{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1741","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Funny Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A sequence of $$$n$$$ numbers is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"permutation"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it contains all numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ exactly once. For example, the sequences $$$[3, 1, 4, 2]$$$, [$$$1$$$] and $$$[2,1]$$$ are permutations, but $$$[1,2,1]$$$, $$$[0,1]$$$ and $$$[1,3,4]$$$ are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a given number $$$n$$$ you need to make a permutation $$$p$$$ such that two requirements are satisfied at the same time:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For each element $$$p_i$$$, at least one of its neighbors has a value that differs from the value of $$$p_i$$$ by one. That is, for each element $$$p_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$), at least one of its neighboring elements (standing to the left or right of $$$p_i$$$) must be $$$p_i + 1$$$, or $$$p_i - 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the permutation must have no fixed points. That is, for every $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$), $$$p_i \\neq i$$$ must be satisfied. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call the permutation that satisfies these requirements "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"funny"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, let $$$n = 4$$$. Then [$$$4, 3, 1, 2$$$] is a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"funny"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation, since: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" to the right of $$$p_1=4$$$ is $$$p_2=p_1-1=4-1=3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" to the left of $$$p_2=3$$$ is $$$p_1=p_2+1=3+1=4$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" to the right of $$$p_3=1$$$ is $$$p_4=p_3+1=1+1=2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" to the left of $$$p_4=2$$$ is $$$p_3=p_4-1=2-1=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" for all $$$i$$$ is $$$p_i \\ne i$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a given positive integer $$$n$$$, output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"funny"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation of length $$$n$$$, or output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"funny"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation of length $$$n$$$ does not exist."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input data contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of f single line containing one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print on a separate line: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"funny"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" or the number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the permutation you are looking for does not exist. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n4\n3\n7\n5\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 4 2 1\n-1\n6 7 4 5 3 2 1\n5 4 1 2 3\n2 1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first test case is explained in the problem statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, it is not possible to make the required permutation: permutations $$$[1, 2, 3]$$$, $$$[1, 3, 2]$$$, $$$[2, 1, 3]$$$, $$$[3, 2, 1]$$$ have fixed points, and in $$$[2, 3, 1]$$$ and $$$[3, 1, 2]$$$ the first condition is met not for all positions."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1741B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1741/problem/B"}